<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The firmware of a bot whose owner wrote none (decision D160). The body
  (floppy.scx) starts a firmware on top of its abilities: the owner's
  document its firmware_src param names, invoked by srcexpr as the child
  "firmware", or, when it names none, this one. It stands in for an
  owner's firmware so the body's topology is the same either way: it
  offers nothing and does nothing. The body never shows it to the
  cognition.

  An owner's firmware is any SCXML document: it is started once its
  session is running (the body reads it with <device:snapshot>, decision
  D242), what it offers is every event a transition without a cond takes
  with an event:schema (the body reads them each turn with
  <decision:offers undeclared="all">), a selection of one of them is sent
  to it (its session id, <body>.firmware), and a
  bot.ability.cognition.input {stimulus} to its parent hands the body an
  observation, which takes a turn as any ability's product does. The body
  reads its state and data model each turn with <device:snapshot>, as it
  reads a device.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="firmware" initial="running">
  <script src="firmware.js"/>
  <state id="running">
    <!-- Whatever reaches it, it takes and does nothing with. -->
    <transition event="*"/>
  </state>
</scxml>
